    "created_at": "2022-03-15T12:24:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-15T12:24:12Z",
    "body": "Firefox is tracking various issues in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1056860.\r\n\r\nIt took me a while, but I think I understand. _inputURLString_ contains a fragment component and the test expected less code points to be percent-encoded during parsing than it should have according to the URL Standard. And this change manifests itself when the parsed _inputURLString_ is eventually serialized and percent-encoded again.\r\n\r\nAnd this only happens from U+0023 (#) onward which explains why U+0020 and U+0022 are not affected in the diff.\r\n\r\nI think that means your fix is correct and there's nothing left to do here (except for Firefox to fix its bug).\r\n\r\ncc @valenting @TimothyGu ",
